request.description:
Graph objects have number of relationships to other objects. As mentioned in the Relationships section, those related objects can be retrieved by sending `GET` requests to the relationship URL.

Some relationships are accesible only to users who have access to Google Threat Intelligence.

The relationships supported by graph objects are documented in the Graph API object page.

```json Response example for owner
{
"data": {
"attributes": {
"first_name": "Richard",
"last_name": "Hendricks",
"profile_phrase": "CEO of Pied Piper",
"reputation": 1,
"status": "active",
"user_since": 1528111032
},
"id": "hendricks",
"links": {
"self": "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/users/hendricks"
},
"type": "user"
},
"links": {
"self": "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/graphs/g510b3e01190b9e6001f7ed7d14015558b11ca9d3e87367b6b809bbb402645bf2/owner"
}
}
```

